legal advice — have a qualified professional review before release.

Recommended options
--------------------
- Proprietary / commercial (typical for a paid Steam game): keep source closed
  or "source-available" with an all-rights-reserved notice like this one.
- If you intend to open-source the engine-side code while keeping art/audio
  proprietary, a common split is:
    * Code:   MIT or Apache-2.0
    * Assets: CC BY-NC-ND 4.0 or a custom proprietary asset license
  Put asset terms in a separate ASSETS-LICENSE file and reference it here.

What is original in this repository
-----------------------------------
All code, the procedural meshes/materials, SVG UI, and synthesized placeholder
audio in this repository are original works created for this project. No
third-party marketplace assets or copyrighted material are included. See
THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md for the (currently empty) third-party inventory and the
engine attribution.

